    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup; his score of 83.29 is the highest of the day, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against Martinez (4.70 xERA) and an elite 14% platoon boost. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** follows closely at 81.47, as he remains a must-start despite facing the left-handed Rod\u00f3n, largely due to a park factor bump and premium positioning in the #2 spot. While our SB scarcity strategy remains paramount, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) presents the most compelling case for an \"impact\" start; beyond his strong projection, he benefits from a slow delivery by Ober, which significantly increases his stolen base upside, a key tactical consideration for our roster construction.\n\nThe decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (44.77) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Vargas** offers a strong xwOBA, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** in the middle infield. The high xERA of opponent McLean was not enough to overcome the superior projected output of our current starters. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (59.92) and **Coby Mayo** (63.53) closely; both benefit from a 16% park factor uplift, but they carry enough volatility that we must remain vigilant if the game state shifts. We continue to navigate the absence of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, placing additional pressure on the remaining depth pieces like **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** to provide value in the back half of the order. \n\nRisk management for the Austin Waves today centers on the opposing arms; specifically, we are exercising caution with **Kyle Tucker** (58.73), whose score is suppressed by the matchup against Bachar. While we expect him to contribute, his sub-60 efficiency score is near our floor threshold, warranting close observation as the game progresses to preserve our precious game 